## The one-stop shop for cross-country macroeconomic data

Macroeconomic statistics are essential for researchers and practitioners. Yet the underlying data are scattered across hundreds of sources, with inconsistent units, country and time coverage, and variable definitions. The result: users spend weeks understanding, cleaning, harmonizing, and combining data before they can do any analysis. [...] If you use the GMD, it must be cited as follows.

```
